eval/results/

# Throwaway probes — a driver script against the running app, or a component
# that exists only to prove a lint rule fires. Written to be deleted. Ignored so
# the Stop hook's `git status` scope does not read one session's scratch file as
# another's unformatted change. A lint probe has to sit under the path its rule
# scopes to, so this covers `.svelte` too.
*.tmp.mjs
*.tmp.ts
*.tmp.svelte
# `scripts/probe-registry.mjs` already exempts "an untracked scratch
# `zz-*.probe.ts` in a dirty tree" from the registry it enforces, so that name
# is the convention for a throwaway probe. It has to be ignored here too, or
# the same file the registry excuses blocks the Stop hook on formatting.
zz*.probe.ts

# The seeded design canvas: ~2 MB of Claude Design's editor, generated by the
# skill's seeder from the `.dc.html` artboards beside it and republished from
# them every time. Not ours to format or review — and its embedded editor code
# trips the citation checker with `AGENTS.md R0`-shaped strings it never wrote.
# The artboards and canvas.json ARE the source; this is the build of them.
docs/redesign-answer-first/*-redesign.html
